Note that any configured {@link Ext.Component#cfg!padding padding} will be ignored on items within a Form layout.

A layout that arranges items horizontally across a Container. This layout optionally divides available horizontal
space between child items containing a numeric `{@link #cfg!flex flex}` configuration.

This layout may also be used to set the heights of child items by configuring it with the {@link #cfg!align #align} option.

    @example
    Ext.create('Ext.Panel', {
        width: 500,
        height: 300,
        title: "HBoxLayout Panel",
        layout: {
            type: 'hbox',
            align: 'stretch'
        },
        renderTo: document.body,
        items: [{
            xtype: 'panel',
            title: 'Inner Panel One',
            flex: 2
        },{
            xtype: 'panel',
            title: 'Inner Panel Two',
            flex: 1
        },{
            xtype: 'panel',
            title: 'Inner Panel Three',
            flex: 1
        }]
